# apple-storefront-clone — environment configuration
#
# This is a client-only single-page app with no backend: there is no database,
# no auth, no payment provider, and no API to configure. The app itself reads
# NO environment variables (verified: zero `import.meta.env` / `process.env`
# references under `src/`).
#
# The one variable below is read by the sitemap generator only
# (scripts/build-sitemap.mjs), which stamps the public origin into
# public/sitemap.xml and public/robots.txt at generation time:
#
#   npm run sitemap
#
# Copy to .env if you want to customize generation; otherwise the documented
# default applies.

# ---- Site -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Public origin of the deployment, written into public/sitemap.xml as the base
# of every route URL and referenced by public/robots.txt's Sitemap directive.
# Default when unset: http://localhost:5173/ (the dev origin).
# For a real deploy, set it to the deployed origin and re-run `npm run sitemap`.
VITE_SITE_URL=http://localhost:5173/

# ---- Optional local PostgreSQL 17 -----------------------------------------
# The repo family's documented local database (see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §4).
# The SPA never connects to it — it is the standard local environment for the
# repo family and future full-stack work. Nothing here is read by this app.
#   Rootless install: bash docs/setup_pg_z.sh
#   Docker alternative: docker compose up -d
#   Connection: postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:5432/app_db
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:5432/app_db
